{"id": "EUVD-2026-103466", "enisaUuid": "aefd0ef0-0e03-3bdc-8d69-2ca0b7359d54", "description": "libtta through 2.3 contains a divide-by-zero vulnerability in tta_decoder_init_get_info() that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying an unvalidated zero sample rate. Attackers can craft a .tta file with a recomputed header CRC32 that triggers SIGFPE, crashing applications including the bundled tta console tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T11:38:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:37:55", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libtta-seek-table-count-overflow-oob-write", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta/blob/af8dc48ce859e98842ab1a3eec98416d22a5199e/libtta.c#L602-L605", "https://sourceforge.net/projects/tta/", "https://github.com/gchudov/libtta", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libtta-through-2.3-divide-by-zero-via-tta-decoder-init-get-info"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112013", "GHSA-phg4-99g6-v62p"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ea7a0454-4ec6-3c6a-9692-18568ce91c1e", "product": {"name": "libtta", "vendor": {"name": "True Audio"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ab5e03b0-3956-3a49-93f8-d53880216047", "vendor": {"name": "True Audio"}}], "isExploited": false}